  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2033}=-1,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(-2)=2,\\,{y}^{\u2032}(0)=0,\\,-2\\le x\\le 0\n$$\n\nThe general solution can be written as\n\n$$\ny=f(x)+B\\cdot g(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $B\\in R$ is arbitrary. \n\nSelect functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ that make this statement true.\n\n$\\,f(x)=$\n{{field-1}} \n$\\,g(x)=$\n{{field-2}}",
